+  {
+    "claim_constructor_ast_identical": true,
+    "submitted_sha256_checked_in_stage2": true,
+    "trusted_regeneration_byte_identical": true
+  }
+  pinning_check_exit=0
+
+The script invokes `kast --sort Module --output json` separately on the
+submitted `solution.mpy` and the initial `Module(...)` extracted from the
+claim. Equality is constructor-level equality, not merely textual whitespace
+normalization.
+
+Command:
+  kprove spec-body-mutation.k
+    --definition /tmp/audit-work/reconstruction-8-sum-product/proof-kompiled
+    --spec-module SUM-PRODUCT-SPEC-BODY-MUTATION
+Exit: 1 (expected)
+Relevant output:
+  Warning (WarnStuckClaimState)
+  #Not ( {
+      productInts ( IS )
+    #Equals
+      sumInts ( IS )
+  } )
+  <result>
+    PyTuple ( PyInt ( productInts ( IS ) ) ,
+              PyInt ( productInts ( IS ) ) ) ~> .K
+  </result>
+  [Error] Prover: backend terminated because the configuration cannot be
+  rewritten further.
+  body_mutation_kprove_exit=1
+
+The mutation changes the actual program term in the claim and changes the
+destination closure consistently; the unchanged intended result is what
+causes failure. A satisfying concrete witness is `IS = 2, 3, .Ints`, for
+which the mutation returns `(6, 6)` but the contract requires `(5, 6)`.
